{"abstract":"Five decades of stomach content data allowed insight into the development of consumption, diet composition, and resulting somatic growth of Gadus morhua (Atlantic cod) in the eastern Baltic Sea. We show a recent reversal in feeding level over body length. Present feeding levels of small cod indicate severe growth limitation and increased starvation-related mortality. For young cod, the low growth rate and the high mortality rate are manifested through a reduction in size-at-age. The low feeding levels are likely the result of a decrease in benthic prey abundance due to increased hypoxic areas, while decreasing abundances of pelagic species in the area of cod distribution have prevented a compensatory shift in diet. Our study emphasizes that environmental forcing and the decline in pelagic prey caused changes in consumption and growth rates of small cod. The food reduction is amplified by stunted growth leading to high densities of cod of smaller size competing for the scarce resources. The average growth rate is negative, and only individuals with feeding levels well above average will survive, though growing slowly. These results suggest that the relation between consumption rate, somatic growth and predatorprey population densities is strongly environmentally mediated.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Neuenfeldt, Stefan","Bartolino, Valerio","Orio, Alessandro","Andersen, Ken Haste","Andersen, Niels Gerner","Niiranen, Susa","Bergström, Ulf","Ustups, Didzis","Kulatska, Nataliia","Casini, Michele"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-333005"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Neuenfeldt, Stefan"],"country":["Latvia","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institute of Food Safety Animal Health and Environment","Stockholm University","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences"],"keyword":["Baltic Sea","Environmental change","GROWTH","Gadus morhua","Predation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feeding and growth of atlantic cod i gadus morhua i l in the eastern baltic sea under environmental change","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85082294563","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-333005","identifier":[{"id":"85082294563","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5f71449b-6e25-403f-b215-d4c9fcd83c22"],"keyword":["Baltic Sea","Bioenergetics modelling","Environmental change","Gadus morhua","Growth","Predation","Stomach data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-8-D33F3C1C25A71E7CEEEDA9491A7703FE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Oceans and Arctic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"swedish university of agricultural sciences","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"lv","key":"institute of food safety animal health and environment","loc":["Latvia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Institute of Food Safety Animal Health and Environment","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stefan","key":"neuenfeldtstefanpau","last":"Neuenfeldt","locid":"3afa675a-36d7-49a9-beff-96ec4af9f54b","name":"Neuenfeldt, Stefan","orcid":"0000-0001-8574-3257","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Valerio","key":"bartolinovaleriopau","last":"Bartolino","name":"Bartolino, Valerio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"orioalessandropau","last":"Orio","name":"Orio, Alessandro","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ken Haste","key":"andersenkenhastepau","last":"Andersen","locid":"af8fa35c-b159-497e-af0b-5f5efc6f245e","name":"Andersen, Ken Haste","orcid":"0000-0002-8478-3430","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Gerner","key":"andersennielsgernerpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"7c410bf7-684b-4408-a855-c92fb73640ee","name":"Andersen, Niels Gerner","orcid":"0000-0002-2560-6071","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Susa","key":"niiranensusapau","last":"Niiranen","name":"Niiranen, Susa","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulf","key":"bergströmulfpau","last":"Bergström","name":"Bergström, Ulf","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Didzis","key":"ustupsdidzispau","last":"Ustups","name":"Ustups, Didzis","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nataliia","key":"kulatskanataliiapau","last":"Kulatska","name":"Kulatska, Nataliia","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"casinimichelepau","last":"Casini","name":"Casini, Michele","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/icesjms/fsz224","issn":["10543139","10959289"],"issn_org":["10543139"],"issue":"2","journal":"I