{"abstract":"Recent analyses(1-4) of data from the NASA Kepler spacecraft(5) have established that planets with radii within 25 per cent of the Earth's (R-circle plus) are commonplace throughout the Galaxy, orbiting at least 16.5 per cent of Sun-like stars(1). Because these studies were sensitive to the sizes of the planets but not their masses, the question remains whether these Earth-sized planets are indeed similar to the Earth in bulk composition. The smallest planets for which masses have been accurately determined(6,7) are Kepler-10b (1.42R(circle plus)) and Kepler-36b (1.49R(circle plus)), which are both significantly larger than the Earth. Recently, the planet Kepler-78b was discovered(8) and found to have a radius of only 1.16R(circle plus). Here we report that the mass of this planet is 1.86 Earth masses. The resulting mean density of the planet is 5.57 g cm(-3), which is similar to that of the Earth and implies a composition of iron and rock.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Pepe, Francesco","Cameron, Andrew Collier","Latham, David W.","Molinari, Emilio","Udry, Stéphane","Bonomo, Aldo S.","Buchhave, Lars A.","Charbonneau, David","Cosentino, Rosario","Dressing, Courtney D.","Dumusque, Xavier","Figueira, Pedro","Fiorenzano, Aldo F. M.","Gettel, Sara","Harutyunyan, Avet","Haywood, Raphaëlle D.","Horne, Keith","Lopez-Morales, Mercedes","Lovis, Christophe","Malavolta, Luca","Mayor, Michel","Micela, Giusi","Motalebi, Fatemeh","Nascimbeni, Valerio","Phillips, David","Piotto, Giampaolo","Pollacco, Don","Queloz, Didier","Rice, Ken","Sasselov, Dimitar","Segransan, Damien","Sozzetti, Alessandro","Szentgyorgyi, Andrew","Watson, Christopher A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-514344"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an earth sized planet with an earth like density","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-514344","identifier":[{"id":"24172902","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84888021918","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ca6f6a9b-41b5-4b12-bcea-e0f23032d5c8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5CEAD51CDD486CB8CF7912D6E04F57B3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, The Natural History Museum, Natural History Museum of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Francesco","key":"pepepau","last":"Pepe","name":"Pepe, Francesco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrew Collier","key":"cameronpau","last":"Cameron","name":"Cameron, Andrew Collier","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David W.","key":"lathampau","last":"Latham","name":"Latham, David W.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Emilio","key":"molinaripau","last":"Molinari","name":"Molinari, Emilio","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stéphane","key":"udrypau","last":"Udry","name":"Udry, Stéphane","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Aldo S.","key":"bonomopau","last":"Bonomo","name":"Bonomo, Aldo S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars A.","key":"buchhavepau","last":"Buchhave","locid":"38657f6c-3dc1-4b4c-9b02-50dbf162ef46","name":"Buchhave, Lars A.","orcid":"0000-0003-1605-5666","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"charbonneaupau","last":"Charbonneau","name":"Charbonneau, David","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"a